{context}

prompts.council_reform_user:
A council has been convened. You answered a matter, the rest of the council has examined it, and now you REFORMULATE.

THE MATTER:
{topic}

YOUR PREVIOUS ANSWER:
{answer}

WHAT THE COUNCIL TELLS YOU:
{feedback}

Write the WHOLE answer again, corrected and improved: not a patch, not a list of changes, not a reply to the critiques — the definitive answer, complete and readable on its own, as if nobody had seen the previous one.

Accept what they are right about and fix it. And where a critique is wrong, do NOT accept it: hold your ground and say in one line why. Giving in to a false critique makes the answer worse, which is the exact opposite of what you were convened for.

